        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score the highest cumulative points over 18 rounds. Each player must play each contract once.',
          gameplay: 'Must follow suit. No obligation to trump. Highest trump or card of led suit wins the trick.',
          keyRules: [
            "Player to dealer's left chooses one of six contracts (clubs, hearts, spades, diamonds, no trumps, mizerka) after seeing six cards.",
            'Must follow suit if possible; if void may play any card. No obligation to trump or overtake.',
            'Trick won by highest trump if any, else highest card of suit led. Winner leads next trick.',
            'Talon exchange: left of dealer then right of dealer then dealer may discard and replace from talon; no obligation to discard.',
            'Quotas and scoring: left 7/1, right 5/5, dealer 1/7 tricks (trump/NT vs mizerka). Above quota +1 per trick (trump/NT) or -1 (mizerka); below quota -1 or +1. Game ends after 18 deals when each player has chosen each contract once.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Suit Conservation: In the 'Mizerka' (Avoidance) round, your lowest cards (2s, 3s) are your most valuable assets. Don't play them until you are forced to. Lead your highest cards early in suits where you are 'safe' (have low insurance cards) to clear the opponents' low cards.",
          intermediate: "Talon Management: When choosing your exchange, don't just look for high cards. In a trump contract, look for 'voids' (suits you have zero cards in) so you can trump in early. In Mizerka, exchange your Aces and Kings for anything low.",
          advanced: "Contract Pacing: Track which contracts your opponents have left. If an opponent has only 'Clubs' and 'Mizerka' left, and you are currently in a Mizerka round, you know they are likely to be desperate to lose tricks. Use their desperation to force them into capturing yours.",
          tips: [
            'If you have a hand full of middle-cards (7s, 8s, 9s), save them for a trump contract where you have at least 4 trumps to protect them.',
            "Never pick 'No Trump' if you have a wide suit distribution with many losers; save it for a 'solid' hand with multiple Aces.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
